From: Cubie A7Z Arch Linux ARM contributors
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sunxi: leave HDMI output state to atomic and PM callbacks

The HPD thread unconditionally disables the transmitter and clears its
private DRM mode state on a disconnect, without updating the committed
CRTC state. On reconnect it only probes the sink and emits a hotplug event.
With the vendor fbdev console there is no client hotplug callback to issue
a modeset, leaving an active CRTC backed by a disabled transmitter. Short
HPD pulses while a sink locks to a new mode expose the same mismatch.

Do not alter the committed mode or transmitter state from the HPD path.
Atomic disable/enable and PM callbacks already own those transitions.
Keep the real HPD detection, sink-cache invalidation and notifications.
This does not force a connector, choose a resolution, or replay an atomic
commit from the HPD thread.

Base: radxa/allwinner-bsp f51e1e6195d4350abc590bff852e213279e660a6
---
--- a/drivers/drm/sunxi_drm_hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/drm/sunxi_drm_hdmi.c
@@ -1399,14 +1399,16 @@
 
 static int _sunxi_drv_hdmi_hpd_plugout(struct sunxi_drm_hdmi *hdmi)
 {
-	int ret = 0;
-
 	hdmi_inf("hdmi drv detect hpd disconnect\n");
 
-	/* clean drm info */
-	hdmi->hdmi_ctrl.drm_enable   = 0x0;
-	hdmi->hdmi_ctrl.drm_mode_set = 0x0;
-	memset(&hdmi->drm_mode, 0x0, sizeof(struct drm_display_mode));
+	/*
+	 * HPD describes the sink connection, not the committed CRTC state.
+	 * Leave the active mode and output to the atomic/PM callbacks: disabling
+	 * the transmitter here leaves an active CRTC with its hardware off.
+	 * A reconnect need not cause another modeset (notably for fbcon).
+	 * The normal HPD notification still lets a modesetting client disable
+	 * the output or select a mode for a different sink.
+	 */
 
 	hdmi->hdmi_ctrl.drv_pixel_format_cap  = 0x0;
 	hdmi->hdmi_ctrl.drv_dynamic_range_cap = 0x0;
@@ -1417,9 +1419,6 @@
 	drm_edid_free(hdmi->hdmi_ctrl.drv_edid_data);
 #endif
 	hdmi->hdmi_ctrl.drv_edid_data = NULL;
-	ret = _sunxi_drv_hdmi_disable(hdmi);
-	if (ret != 0)
-		hdmi_err("sunxi hdmi driver disable failed when plugout.\n");
 
 	return 0;
 }
